Kurobayomi
Copyright the Kurobayomi contributors.

Kurobayomi is a Rust and GTK4 rewrite of Aniyomi, which is a fork of Mihon (formerly Tachiyomi).
It reimplements their behaviour from their public source code and keeps their licence terms.

Aniyomi   https://github.com/aniyomiorg/aniyomi   Apache License 2.0
Mihon     https://github.com/mihonapp/mihon        Apache License 2.0
Tachiyomi https://github.com/tachiyomiorg/tachiyomi Apache License 2.0

The app's icons (src/theme/icons/scalable/actions) are Material Design icons by Google, recoloured for GTK:
Material Design Icons https://github.com/google/material-design-icons Apache License 2.0

The colour choices of the Appearance page (src/theme/colours.rs) use the colours of these palettes:
Tokyo Night https://github.com/tokyo-night/tokyo-night-vscode-theme MIT License
Catppuccin  https://github.com/catppuccin/palette                   MIT License
Dracula     https://github.com/dracula/dracula-theme                MIT License
Nord        https://github.com/nordtheme/nord                       MIT License
Gruvbox     https://github.com/morhetz/gruvbox                      MIT/X11 License
Rosé Pine   https://github.com/rose-pine/neovim                     MIT License

The full licence text is in LICENSE.
